    "title": "Increase the number of real time signals. Two is not enough.",
    "problem_statement": "sigset_t is a uint32_t which limits NuttX to 32 signals. This PR converts sigset_t to an array of uint32_t to support 64 signals (including 32 real-time signals), matching Linux. Adds SIGSET_FMT and SIGSET_ELEM() macros for portable signal set printing. nuttx-apps PR #1682 updates ostest to use these new macros and a new sigset_isequal() helper.",
